Independent corroboration of the hda_multi_out ABI fix
------------------------------------------------------
The fork at https://github.com/fbottarel/aw88399-hda-dkms (branch legion-fix)
reached the identical one-line conclusion about struct hda_multi_out roughly ten
weeks before this tree did:

  1c4f2a8  2026-08-28  "common: fix struct hda_multi_out layout drift causing
                        NULL deref crash"
  82bd903  2026-09-03  carries the applied change to common/hda_local.h, plus a
                        partial Legion fixup body (the DAC 0x02 override only)

Credit for the independent diagnosis belongs to that fork and its contributors.
Our work was arrived at separately, via kernel BTF and pahole; two forks landing
on the same missing member is the strongest argument that this is an upstream
defect rather than a local misconfiguration.

That fork takes a different architectural route for the rest: it keeps
snd_intel_dspcfg.dsp_driver=3 and solves the resulting loss of the internal
microphone by diverting the distribution's HDA UCM2 configuration. That is a
legitimate alternative to the approach here, which stays on the legacy HDA path
and needs no boot parameter and no diverted system files. It does not fix the
SND_PCI_QUIRK/HDA_CODEC_QUIRK mismatch (fix 5), so its quirk entries cannot match
a 16IAX10H's controller SSID; it does not sign modules; and it leaves
AUTOINSTALL="yes".

Local changes against 7c307da (see "What we changed" in README.md):
  Makefile              module names may not contain '/' on kernel 6.16+
  soc-codecs/aw88399.h  snd_soc_kcontrol_component() shim for kernel 7.0
  common/hda_local.h    restore struct hda_multi_out::share_spdif_kctl (ABI fix)
  realtek/alc269.c      port the real Legion fixup body; SND_PCI_QUIRK -> HDA_CODEC_QUIRK
  dkms.conf             BUILT_MODULE_LOCATION; AUTOINSTALL=no;
                        PACKAGE_VERSION=1.0-legion1 so this tree cannot collide
                        in /usr/src with upstream's 1.0 or fbottarel's 1.0.2
  new                   preflight-abi-check.sh, install-dkms-signed.sh,
                        uninstall-dkms.sh, README.md

Upstream's install.sh and make_deb.sh are intentionally NOT redistributed here:
install.sh produces unsigned modules that Secure Boot silently refuses, and
make_deb.sh sets snd_intel_dspcfg.dsp_driver=3, which breaks this hardware.

